// Furniture whose picture is its own: the frame a table is built on.
//
// One family of `tfs/assets/sprites.ron`'s roster. Every .ron in this
// directory is baked, in FILE-NAME order and then expansion order, so
// the atlas layout is a function of the manifest and not of the
// filesystem. Two files claiming one sprite name is a bake error.
//
// It sits beside 90-smooth-structures.ron rather than in it because the
// distinction that file is named for is the whole distinction: a table
// wears one of forty-seven frames chosen by its neighbours, and a table
// frame wears one picture chosen by nothing. tg draws it off the
// general structures sheet for the same reason -- four legs standing on
// their own are not part of a row (`/obj/structure/table_frame`,
// code/game/objects/structures/table_frames.dm:12-17).
(
    // Sheet aliases are local to this family; @names below resolve here.
    sheets: [
        ("structures", "obj/structures.dmi"),
    ],
    sprites: [
        ("table_frame", Dmi("@structures", "table_frame", 0)),
    ],
)
